The `## [Unreleased]` section of CHANGES.md against the editorial convention stated in
docs/agent-notes/conventions.md (gh-ocannl-807). Released sections are history and are not
read; the counts scanned go to stderr, since a tally in a golden moves on every editorial
pass (gh-ocannl-665).

CHANGES.md carries exactly one `## [Unreleased]` heading: true
every line in Unreleased is blank, a subheading, a bullet, or a two-space continuation: true
every continuation line in Unreleased belongs to a bullet: true
every Unreleased bullet is at most three lines: true
every Unreleased bullet cites gh-ocannl-NNN or a staging PR #NNN: true
the section reader finds the eleven synthetic control bullets: true
the length rule flags a synthetic four-line bullet: true
the length rule flags a bullet whose fourth line follows a blank one: true
the citation rule flags a synthetic uncited bullet: true
the citation rule flags an unqualified `PR #NNN`: true
the citation rule flags a repository name not qualifying the PR number: true
the citation rule flags an issue number running into a typo: true
the citation rule flags a PR number running into a typo: true
the citation rule flags a repository run into `PR #` with no separator: true
the citation rule flags an issue prefix embedded in another token: true
both rules pass a bullet citing a staging PR: true
both rules pass a bullet citing a gh-ocannl issue: true
the gate refuses every shape this grammar does not name: true
the gate accepts every shape it names: true
the gate refuses a continuation with no bullet above it: true
the section reader refuses a changelog with two Unreleased anchors: true
only the exact `## [Unreleased]` line counts as the anchor: true
an indented copy of the anchor's text is not the anchor: true
a four-space-indented copy of the anchor is code, not a second anchor: true
an anchor quoted in a fence or a comment is not a second anchor: true
an anchor quoted inside a longer fence stays inert: true
a backtick fence's info string may not contain a backtick: true
an anchor inside released raw HTML is not a second anchor: true
an unrelated closing tag leaves a raw HTML block open: true
a raw HTML block that closes on its opening line hides nothing after it: true
a tag merely starting with a raw-HTML name is a generic block, ending at the blank line: true
an autolink opens no HTML block, so the heading after it is still structure: true
a comment opener inside a code span is literal text, not an HTML comment: true
a level-4 subheading stays inside Unreleased, and the released section does not: true

